# Pairs with MovedStreamKeepsAckedWrites. When the lease lapses the source
# activation simply stops refusing appends, without releasing the durable fence
# in the registry first, so the flip - which finds the fence still held - goes
# ahead and discards the writes it acknowledged meanwhile. The base serves
# unfenced only after the release, which the flip's compare-and-swap observes.
MODULE: MovedStreamKeepsAckedWritesLapseUnfencesWithoutRelease
TARGET: MovedStreamKeepsAckedWrites
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a lapsed lease unfences the source without releasing the durable fence, so a flip still succeeds
PERTURBS: LeaseLapse

--- FIND
    /\ lapsed' = TRUE
    /\ UNCHANGED <<next, inflight, durable, tail, acked, cons, move, moveCopy, dfence, afence, moves, crashes, coordCrashes>>
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the activation serves unfenced as soon as the lease lapses.
    /\ lapsed' = TRUE
    /\ afence' = FALSE
    /\ UNCHANGED <<next, inflight, durable, tail, acked, cons, move, moveCopy, dfence, moves, crashes, coordCrashes>>
--- END